guide forever/reputation/ironforge
title Ironforge Reputation
category Reputation
folder Reputation · Cities
faction Alliance
levels 12-60
zone Ironforge
keywords Ironforge, Mistina Steelshield, cloth quartermaster, Additional Runecloth, Wool, Silk, Mageweave, Runecloth, ram, Swift Gray Ram, grey quests, Coldridge Valley, Kharanos, Dun Morogh, Oralius, Morgan's Vigil, Blackrock Medallion, Enraged Wildkin, Alterac Valley
reward text Exalted with Ironforge: in Classic, other races may buy the rams
reward text About 600 Ironforge reputation from level 52-59 quests in the Burning Steppes and Winterspring; Alterac Valley's quests pay Ironforge too
reward text About 2,900 Ironforge reputation from low-level quests in Dun Morogh, most of it paid to Gnomeregan too (in Classic, a fifth of it at 60)
why Cloth, the Burning Steppes quests and the Dun Morogh hubs, which pay Gnomeregan too; Alterac Valley adds more.

# Built from Forever's quest data (the reputation each quest pays, as Forever's
# quest pages give it), quests.json, npcs.json and items.json (givers, drops,
# farm spots), and the Forever client tables (Faction: Dwarves start at 4000,
# Humans, Night Elves and Gnomes at 3100, Alliance Skyborne at 2000;
# ItemSparse: no item needs Ironforge standing, and the rams carry no
# reputation requirement in the client).
# Numbers: the first donation of each cloth pays 150 (60 cloth); Additional
# Runecloth (7806) pays 50 for 20 Runecloth and repeats. Bands: Friendly 6000,
# Honored 12000, Revered 21000.
# Low-level quests: in Classic a quest 6+ levels below you pays a fifth less per
# level, down to a fifth; one Forever beta report saw full pay at level 30.
# Gnomeregan Exiles the same amount (see that guide: one sweep, two factions).
# The quest hubs are optional: each hub's first step carries a label, the
# steps after it run only when it was done (`when done`), so skipping the
# first step skips the hub.
# Level 52-59 quests first (they pay in full at 60, or nearly): Royal
# Historian Archesonus's Thaurissan relics (3702, 3701: 110), Oralius at
# Morgan's Vigil (3823-3825, 4283: 400) and Enraged Wildkin in Winterspring
# (6604-4864: 100). Left to a tip: the Blackrock Depths quests (Kharan
# Mighthammer 100, The Fate of the Kingdom 150, The Good Stuff 100) and
# Alterac Valley, whose one-time quests pay Ironforge as much as Stormpike
# (1,870 in Forever's quest pages; Classic pays Ironforge for them too) and whose
# Irondeep and Coldtooth Supplies (25 per 10) and Crystal Cluster (50 per 5)
# pay only Ironforge. Nefarian's head pays 200 to every Alliance city.
# ASSUMED: other races buy the rams at Exalted with Ironforge (Classic flow;
# Forever's data has no vendor rule for it). In-game check: Veron
# Amberstill's stock for a non-Dwarf at Exalted and below.
# INGAME: grey-quest rep at 60 (Classic: a fifth from 9 levels below; one Forever beta report: full, quest 456 at level 30 paid 100)
# INGAME: reputation discount (Classic: 10% at Honored with the vendor's faction; Forever guide sites report 5% at Friendly rising to 20% at Exalted, another says unannounced). Check a city vendor's price at Friendly and at Honored.
# Legacy Diplomat adds up to 10% to every gain; the numbers here leave it out.
# No race has a reputation bonus in Forever (Diplomacy is gone).

step Mistina Steelshield, the cloth quartermaster
  tip Mistina Steelshield takes cloth for Ironforge; she stands outside the clothier on the north side of the Great Forge, among the tailors. Each first donation of 60 Wool, Silk, Mageweave and Runecloth pays 150 reputation once; after the Runecloth one, Additional Runecloth pays 50 for every 20 Runecloth, as often as you like. The Auction House in the Commons is the quickest source of cloth. In Classic, quests pay full reputation while they are at most 5 levels below you, so do Dun Morogh (levels 1-12), Loch Modan (10-20) and the Wetlands (20-30) while you level through them. After the donations come the level 52-59 quests of the Burning Steppes and Winterspring (about 600), then the optional Dun Morogh hubs, best rate first: Coldridge Valley (about 37 a minute at full value), Kharanos (26), the quarry (17). Every Ironforge gain also gives a quarter as much to Stormwind, Darnassus and the Gnomeregan Exiles, except quests in the level 1-10 start areas. Legacy Diplomat adds up to 10% to every gain.
  level 12
  collect 2592 x60 nearest            -- Wool Cloth: troggs, gnolls and kobolds in Loch Modan and the Wetlands
  accept 7802
  turnin 7802

step A Donation of Silk
  tip Silk Cloth drops from humanoids level 23 to 40: the Dragonmaw of the Wetlands, the Syndicate of Alterac and Arathi, Stranglethorn's trolls.
  level 26
  collect 4306 x60 nearest
  accept 7803
  turnin 7803

step A Donation of Mageweave
  tip Mageweave Cloth drops from humanoids level 35 to 50: the Shadowforge and Dark Iron dwarves of the Badlands and Searing Gorge, the Dunemaul ogres of Tanaris, the Hatecrest naga of Feralas.
  level 40
  collect 4338 x60 nearest
  accept 7804
  turnin 7804

step A Donation of Runecloth
  tip Runecloth drops from humanoids level 50 and up: the Scourge cultists and Scarlet Crusade in the Plaguelands, the Deadwood furbolgs of Felwood, the Winterfall furbolgs of Winterspring. Keep any Runecloth past the first 60 for Additional Runecloth.
  level 50
  collect 14047 x60 nearest
  accept 7805
  turnin 7805

step Ironforge: Royal Historian Archesonus
  zone Ironforge
  tip These quests are level 52 to 59, so they pay in full at 60, or nearly: about 600 Ironforge reputation (in Classic about 450 at 60, as the Burning Steppes ones are level 52 to 54). Royal Historian Archesonus stands beside King Magni in the High Seat; he sends you to the ruins of Thaurissan in the Burning Steppes.
  level 55
  accept 3702                         -- The Smoldering Ruins of Thaurissan, +10
  kill 8879 quest 3702.1 "Hear Royal Historian Archesonus out"
  turnin 3702
  accept 3701                         -- The Smoldering Ruins of Thaurissan, +100

step Morgan's Vigil: Oralius
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Morgan's Vigil sits in the south-east of the Burning Steppes, at the top of the pass up from Redridge. Oralius wants the Firegut ogres of Dreadmaul Rock, north of the Vigil, thinned out; the Brutes keep to the rock's east side.
  accept 4283                         -- FIFTY! YEP!, +100
  accept 3823                         -- Extinguish the Firegut, +100
  kill 7034 x15 quest 3823.1          -- Firegut Ogre Mage
  kill 7033 x15 quest 3823.2          -- Firegut Ogre
  kill 7035 x7 quest 3823.3           -- Firegut Brute
  turnin 3823
  accept 3824                         -- Gor'tesh the Brute Lord, +100

step Thaurissan and Blackrock Stronghold
  tip The Thaurissan relics are the carved stones in the ruins around Flame Crest, west along the road: click twelve of them. Gor'tesh and the Blackrock orcs and worgs hold the camps at the foot of Blackrock Mountain, further west; each may drop a Blackrock Medallion (about one kill in three), and Oralius wants fifty. The orcs are level 50 and up, so they drop Runecloth too: keep it for Additional Runecloth.
  interact 153556 quest 3701.1        -- Thaurissan Relic
  collect 11080 quest 3824.1          -- Gor'tesh's Lopped Off Head
  collect 11467 x50 quest 4283.1      -- Blackrock Medallion

step Morgan's Vigil: hand in
  tip Plant Gor'tesh's head on the soft dirt mound at the top of Dreadmaul Rock.
  turnin 4283
  turnin 3824
  accept 3825                         -- Ogre Head On A Stick = Party, +100
  interact 160840 quest 3825.1        -- Soft Dirt Mound
  turnin 3825

step Ironforge: Archesonus again
  zone Ironforge
  tip With a group, Blackrock Depths pays more: Archesonus's chain goes on with Kharan Mighthammer (100) and The Fate of the Kingdom (Emperor Thaurissan, 150), and Oralius takes 20 Dark Iron Fanny Packs from the dwarves inside (The Good Stuff, 100). Alterac Valley, from level 51, pays Ironforge too: its one-time quests about 1,900 as your Stormpike standing grows (the Alterac Valley guide walks them), and inside the battle 25 for every 10 Irondeep or Coldtooth Supplies and 50 for 5 Storm Crystals, as often as you like.
  turnin 3701

step Winterspring: Enraged Wildkin
  zone Winterspring
  tip Harlo Wigglesworth in Everlook sends you west to Jaron Stoneshaper at Starfall Village. Jaron's damaged crate and wrecked wagon lie at Mazthoril, down the valley to the south-east; his supplies lie around the wagon and the owlbeasts nearby carry his amulet. The last quest is level 59: 100 Ironforge in full.
