step Additional Runecloth to Honored
  zone Ironforge
  tip Additional Runecloth: 50 reputation for 20 Runecloth, as often as you like. After the four first donations a Human, Night Elf or Gnome stands at Friendly 700 of 6,000, so Honored is 5,300 away: 106 turn-ins, 2,120 Runecloth (Dwarves start 900 higher: 88 turn-ins; Skyborne start at Neutral 2,000, so 6,400 away: 128, two fewer after Exploring the Alliance). The level 52-59 quests above take 12 turn-ins off; each Dun Morogh hub you did takes 10 to 26 more off if it paid in full. More hubs pay Ironforge, in full while they are no more than 5 levels below you: Thelsamar in Loch Modan (about 3,500 in all) and Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands (about 2,500). From level 51 Alterac Valley's one-time quests add about 1,900. Every city gain also gives a quarter as much to the other three Alliance cities (not counted here). Hand in all your Runecloth at once.
  collect 14047 x20 optional nearest
  turnin 7806 direct optional
  rep 47 Honored

step Additional Runecloth to Revered
  tip Honored: in Classic Ironforge's vendors take 10% off for you, Veron Amberstill's rams (20g, the swift ones 200g) included; Forever has not settled it, and guide sites report 5% at Friendly rising to 20% at Exalted. Honored to Revered is 12,000 reputation: 240 turn-ins, 4,800 Runecloth.
  collect 14047 x20 optional nearest
  turnin 7806 direct optional
  rep 47 Revered

step Additional Runecloth to Exalted
  tip Revered to Exalted is 21,000 reputation: 420 turn-ins, 8,400 Runecloth. At Exalted, Veron Amberstill at Amberstill Ranch in eastern Dun Morogh sells his rams to other races in Classic; the Ram and Swift Ram guides cover them.
  collect 14047 x20 optional nearest
  turnin 7806 direct optional
  rep 47 Exalted
